            "section_padding": 20,
            "content_gap": 20,
            "subheading": "THE SCIENCE OF LIFE",
            "heading": "What is Ayurveda?",
            "text": "<p><strong>Ayurveda, the ancient “science of life,” is a 5,000-year-old tradition born in India.</strong><br/><br/>More than a system of healing, it is a philosophy—a way of living in harmony with nature and oneself.</p><p>At its essence, Ayurveda teaches that our health—including the health of our hair—is governed by a balance of three natural energies, called <strong>doshas</strong>: Vata, Pitta, and Kapha.</p><p>When these energies are out of balance, it often shows in our hair—whether through dryness, breakage, thinning, or excess oil. Ayurveda helps restore harmony using herbs, oils, and rituals tailored to your body’s unique needs.</p><p>At <strong>SEVA</strong>, we draw from this timeless heritage to craft rituals that are as luxurious as they are grounding. Each drop is a modern expression of Ayurveda—clean, conscious, and designed to nourish not just the hair, but the soul.</p>",
